<title>JAPAN: KDD shares rise on cellular phone plans.</title>
<headline>KDD shares rise on cellular phone plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kokusai Denshin Denwa Co Ltd (KDD) jumped on Monday morning on the news that it plans to apply for government approval on use of radio frequencies in 1999 to enter the next-generation cellular phone business, traders said.</p>
<p>The shares of Japan's top international call carrier gained 240 yen to trade at 8,140 yen at 0149 GMT. Its trading volume was 46,500 shares.</p>
</text>
